<BaseLayout title="About Veldeonix Labs" description="What Veldeonix Labs builds, who maintains it, and how the platform approaches tools, content, privacy, and transparency." canonical="/about/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="narrow"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>About</span></div><h1>About Veldeonix Labs</h1><p>An independent digital platform for practical online tools and supporting guides.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-tight"><article class="narrow prose"><h2>What we build</h2><p>Veldeonix creates focused tools for developers, marketers, and digital creators. The initial collection includes data utilities, advertising calculators, writing helpers, secure generators, and other browser-based utilities.</p><p>Core tools do not require an account. Where practical, processing happens locally in the browser so users do not need to submit the underlying input to a Veldeonix processing server.</p><h2>Who runs Veldeonix</h2><p>Veldeonix Labs is created and maintained by <a href="/authors/fajar-hidayatuloh/">Fajar Hidayatuloh</a>. It is presented as an independent platform, not as a large corporation or professional advisory firm.</p><h2>How content is produced</h2><p>Guides explain the methods, formulas, standards, and limitations behind tools. Factual claims are reviewed before publication and primary sources are preferred when they materially support the topic. AI-assisted software may support research organization, language review, code work, or drafting, but published material receives human review.</p><h2>Transparency</h2><p>Each tool states how it processes data. Calculators show their formulas. Policy pages describe analytics, advertising, corrections, and editorial practices. If the technical behavior changes, the disclosure should change with it.</p></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
